course: dictionary
lesson: 83
title: Activity: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word activity can mean three different things. Read the words around it to find out which one the writer means. The context tells you.
explain: Often activity means something you do for fun, learning or exercise, like «after-school activities». Sometimes it means a place or time when lots of people are busy and moving, like «a lot of activity in the playground». In science, activity can mean things happening in nature, like «volcanic activity».
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does it still make sense? If «physical activity» means exercise that keeps your body healthy, then «Activity makes the heart, lungs, muscles and bones stronger» makes sense. That is how you know you have got it right.
fact: Activity is a noun. Its plural is activities.
fact: An activity can be something you do for fun, learning or exercise.
fact: Activity can also mean a busy situation, with lots of people moving about.
fact: In science, «volcanic activity» and «brain activity» mean things happening inside nature or the body.
fact: Useful phrases include «outdoor activities», «physical activity», «activity book» and «activity sheet».
exercise: «Most of the Earth's volcanic activity happens unseen on the ocean floor.» What does volcanic activity mean here? | *Things happening inside the Earth, such as eruptions | A quiz about the ocean | A volcano painted in bright colours | A day at the beach
exercise: «Blended families get on better when they find shared activities.» What is a shared activity? | A fight between two people | Something you do alone in bed | A type of sleeping bag | *Something two or more people do together
exercise: «Activity makes the heart, lungs, muscles and bones stronger.» What does this sentence tell you activity does? | Stops you from moving at all | Makes you sleepy all day | *Keeps the body strong and healthy | Makes your bones heavier
test: In «a lot of activity in the playground», what does activity mean? | A broken swing | Quiet time with nobody around | *Lots of people busy and moving | A kind of playground game
test: Which of these is an example of an activity you do for fun or learning? | A dark, empty room | A sleepy afternoon | A cloud in the sky | *An activity book
exam: Which sentence uses activity to mean something you do for fun or learning? | *Our class has group activities every Friday | The sky was grey and wet | The playground was quiet and empty all day | The bus arrived late this morning
